  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466320",
      "title": "How Does Angular Interact With Backends?",
      "lectureOrder": 577,
      "videoOrder": 530,
      "sourceHash": "706ca9cc29425c75ce0b8637ad56d27c26da4e864dddde90a874675fc44ee183",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 5.04,
          "en": "-: So how does Angular connect to a database, or how",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.04,
          "end": 8.58,
          "en": "do you connect Angular to a database in your application?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.58,
          "end": 11.82,
          "en": "Well, of course it is a use case that you will often have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.82,
          "end": 15.33,
          "en": "In your Angular app you generate data like posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.33,
          "end": 18.27,
          "en": "or recipes or whatever you have in your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.27,
          "end": 20.58,
          "en": "and you wanna store that data in a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.58,
          "end": 23.73,
          "en": "and all the fetches from there when your app restarts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.73,
          "end": 26.67,
          "en": "when a user revisits your page, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.67,
          "end": 28.23,
          "en": "And it doesn't matter which kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.23,
          "end": 29.73,
          "en": "of database we're talking about,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.73,
          "end": 34.11,
          "en": "if that's a SQL or no SQL database, doesn't really matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.11,
          "end": 36.99,
          "en": "The thing is you don't connect Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.99,
          "end": 38.7,
          "en": "to a database directly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.7,
          "end": 41.67,
          "en": "That means you don't enter your database credentials",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.67,
          "end": 44.1,
          "en": "into your Angular app or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.1,
          "end": 46.2,
          "en": "This would be highly insecure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.2,
          "end": 48.99,
          "en": "because everyone can read your Angular code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.99,
          "end": 51.81,
          "en": "Since it's a frontend JavaScript application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.81,
          "end": 55.02,
          "en": "everyone can inspect the code there, and that is fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.02,
          "end": 56.46,
          "en": "but that also means you must not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.46,
          "end": 58.83,
          "en": "store credentials in there, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.83,
          "end": 61.14,
          "en": "And you will learn how you can still authenticate users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.14,
          "end": 63.48,
          "en": "and so on later in the authentication section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 63.48,
          "end": 67.05,
          "en": "but you definitely don't want to store database credentials.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.05,
          "end": 70.68,
          "en": "For more information on how secure your JavaScript code is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.68,
          "end": 72.09,
          "en": "you can have a look at an article",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 72.09,
          "end": 74.85,
          "en": "and a video I attach to this video here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.85,
          "end": 77.22,
          "en": "So if we don't connect directly to a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.22,
          "end": 78.6,
          "en": "what else can we do then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 78.6,
          "end": 80.19,
          "en": "Because we certainly don't want to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 80.19,
          "end": 83.913,
          "en": "our standalone independent, unconnected Angular app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.78,
          "end": 87.6,
          "en": "Well, you send HTTP requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 87.6,
          "end": 91.08,
          "en": "and you get HTTP responses to and from a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.08,
          "end": 94.74000000000001,
          "en": "A server, in the end, is defined as an API here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.74000000000001,
          "end": 96.75,
          "en": "That means it is, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.75,
          "end": 100.95,
          "en": "a REST API or a GraphQL API you are communicating with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.95,
          "end": 103.17,
          "en": "And in this course, we'll use a REST API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 103.17,
          "end": 106.59,
          "en": "which is the most common form of API you work with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.59,
          "end": 111.09,
          "en": "Now, such a API in the end is almost like a normal website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.09,
          "end": 115.38,
          "en": "but when you visit its URLs, you're not getting back HTML,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.38,
          "end": 118.92,
          "en": "but you're getting back data, mostly in adjacent format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.92,
          "end": 121.74,
          "en": "And if you wanna learn more about REST APIs in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.74,
          "end": 123.48,
          "en": "you also find some helpful resources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.48,
          "end": 125.46,
          "en": "related to that attached to this video,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.46,
          "end": 128.16,
          "en": "and I have a whole course, my Note JS course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.16,
          "end": 130.92,
          "en": "where I also teach you how to create such APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.92,
          "end": 132.48,
          "en": "Because you don't use Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 132.48,
          "end": 134.55,
          "en": "for the creation of these APIs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 134.55,
          "end": 138.45,
          "en": "you use server side languages like Note JS or PHP instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.45,
          "end": 141.93,
          "en": "But you can communicate with these APIs with Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.93,
          "end": 145.2,
          "en": "and on that server, you then can have code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 145.2,
          "end": 149.4,
          "en": "that does interact with a database to store and fetch data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 149.4,
          "end": 151.62,
          "en": "And of course, there are more reasons for communicating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 151.62,
          "end": 155.13,
          "en": "with a server than for storing or fetching data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 155.13,
          "end": 157.32,
          "en": "It's not just about database access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 157.32,
          "end": 158.88,
          "en": "You could be uploading files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 158.88,
          "end": 160.89,
          "en": "or you could be sending some analytics",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 160.89,
          "end": 163.59,
          "en": "to a backend or any other reason",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 163.59,
          "end": 167.82,
          "en": "for why you might need to talk to some backend server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 167.82,
          "end": 170.97,
          "en": "Now in this module, we will not write such a backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 170.97,
          "end": 173.46,
          "en": "from scratch since this is way beyond the scope",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 173.46,
          "end": 177.03,
          "en": "of the course, and totally not Angular's job.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 177.03,
          "end": 180.18,
          "en": "But I will show you how to use a free dummy backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 180.18,
          "end": 181.98,
          "en": "which could of course be replaced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 181.98,
          "end": 184.05,
          "en": "by any real backend you have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 184.05,
          "end": 187.833,
          "en": "cue send requests to use responses and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
